<title>CROATIA: Croatia central bank sells HRK 151.5 mln bills.</title>
<headline>Croatia central bank sells HRK 151.5 mln bills.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia's central bank sold 151.5 million kuna in 35- and 91-day bills on Wednesday, compared to 279 million last week.</p>
<p>Most of the trade, or 141 million, was made in 35-day bills but only 22 million were new signings.</p>
<p>The 35-day bills were granted at an unchanged 7.0 percent and the 91-day bills at an unchanged 8.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Davor Huic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
